 r←Test_CheckVersions_061(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;dir;rc;msg;url;data
⍝ Run CheckForLaterVersion on an installed version that is ahead of everything the Registry hosts.\\
⍝ That is what a beta becomes once it has been published, installed, and then deleted again: the
⍝ Registry still knows the package name, so it answers with the best version of the major version
⍝ line - which is *older* than what is installed. Reporting that as an update, which comparing the
⍝ two IDs for being different rather than for being later once did, offers a downgrade.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 dir←∆GetTempDir''
 dir ⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊣∆TEMP_TEST_DATA,'/myproj/*'

⍝ The local Registry hosts "example-versions" from 0.1.0 to 2.0.0, so it knows the package name but
⍝ not 1.99.0, and every 1.x it offers is earlier than that
 url←Reg.AddSlash ∆TEMP_REGISTRY_FOLDER
 (⊂url ∆BuildList'example-versions-1.99.0')⎕NPUT(dir,'/packages/',Reg.BuildListFilename)1

 data←TC.CheckForLaterVersion dir,'/packages'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢data
 →T.GoToTidyUp'<<< Not available any more >>>'≢⊃data[1;2]   ⍝ nothing earlier may be offered here
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1∊data[;4]               ⍝ nothing to check: the version is gone rather than outdated

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce dir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
